                Baseline rules, bench entry points, retirement decision, and preopt
                ladder/flamegraph observations exist as live AKR heads; akr check is clean
                after akr build.
                """
            method command
            command "akr check"
            verified_by [
                @jpegxl-rs.evidence.performance-md-akr-check-at-head/1,
                @jpegxl-rs.evidence.performance-md-recheck-opt-p/1
            ]
        }
        check stub-only {
            statement """
                JPXL/docs/PERFORMANCE.md is a short stub pointing at AKR observation keys
                and .agent/scratch paths, without duplicated baseline tables or full rules.
                """
            method observation
            verified_by [
                @jpegxl-rs.evidence.performance-md-recheck-opt-p/1,
                @jpegxl-rs.evidence.performance-md-stub-at-head/1
            ]
        }
    }
    implements [
        @jpegxl-rs.decision.retire-performance-md,
        @jpegxl-rs.policy.jpxl-bench-entry-points,
        @jpegxl-rs.policy.performance-baseline-rules
    ]
    supersedes [ @jpegxl-rs.work.dispose-performance-md/1 ]
}

record jpegxl-rs.work.encoder-optimization-plan/1 : work {
    title "Encoder optimization plan of record"
    state proposed
    intent """
        Authoritative plan for jpegxl-rs.track.encoder-optimization: execute Opt-F
        through Opt-P in after-order, supported by the static advisor assessment and
        the optimization decisions and gates.
        """
    implements [
        @jpegxl-rs.decision.optimization-ordering,
        @jpegxl-rs.decision.optimization-pass-opened
    ]
    plan_of_record [ @jpegxl-rs.track.encoder-optimization ]
    supported_by [ @jpegxl-rs.assessment.encoder-static-optimization ]
    source {
        kind legacy
        path "JPXL/optimization-plan.akr"
        excerpt """
            Recommended implementation order: Common foundation; Modular track; VarDCT
            track; parallel and SIMD; LTO and PGO.
            """
    }
}

record jpegxl-rs.work.opt-benches-and-counters/1 : work {
    title "Add encode benches and multiplicity counters"
    state completed
    intent """
        Implement the Opt-F measurement foundation: three encode entry points, optional
        single-probe VarDCT, feature-gated or tooling-side multiplicity counters, and
        first promoted baseline observations under
        @jpegxl-rs.policy.performance-baseline-rules (full logs in .agent/scratch/).
        Keep research scaffolding out of the normative decode path.
        """
    implements [
        @jpegxl-rs.decision.optimization-ordering,
        @jpegxl-rs.policy.jpxl-bench-entry-points,
        @jpegxl-rs.policy.performance-baseline-rules,
        @jpegxl-rs.policy.research-out-of-core
    ]
    part_of [ @jpegxl-rs.milestone.m-opt-foundation ]
}

record jpegxl-rs.work.opt-bulk-bitwriter/1 : work {
    title "Bulk BitWriter write_bits and bitspan append"
    state completed
    intent """
        Replace bit-at-a-time write_bits with bulk LSB packing; add reserve and
        append_bitspan; fix modular append_bits clone-and-replay; keep byte-identical
        output.
        """
    implements [
        @jpegxl-rs.decision.optimization-determinism-contract,
        @jpegxl-rs.policy.optimization-correctness-gates
    ]
    part_of [ @jpegxl-rs.milestone.m-opt-bitwriter ]
}

record jpegxl-rs.work.opt-p-coarse-section-parallel/1 : work {
    title "Opt-P coarse section parallelism (std::thread, Contract A)"
    state completed
    intent """
        Introduce EncodeResources with a groups axis and ordered_map over
        independent LF/pass-group section bodies using std::thread::scope (no
        Rayon dep). Reduce in fixed F.3.1 index order so 1-thread and N-thread
        modular and VarDCT multi-group encodes are byte-identical. Leaf SIMD
        deferred to a follow-up after profiles; LTO/PGO still last.
        """
    acceptance {
        check thread-byte-identity {
            statement """
                multi_section_modular_is_byte_identical_across_thread_counts and
                multi_group_vardct_is_byte_identical_across_thread_counts pass.
                """
            method command
            command "cd JPXL && cargo test -p jpxl-encode multi_section_modular_is_byte_identical --lib && cargo test -p jpxl-encode-policy multi_group_vardct_is_byte_identical --lib"
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.opt-p-thread-byte-identity-at-head/1 ]
        }
    }
    part_of [ @jpegxl-rs.milestone.m-opt-parallel-simd ]
}

record jpegxl-rs.work.opt-plan-import/1 : work {
    title "Disposition advisor optimization-plan.akr into the ledger"
    state proposed
    intent """
        Track migration of JPXL/optimization-plan.akr durable claims into assessment,
        track, decisions, policy, milestones, and work. Complete when every durable
        claim is proposed or explicitly declined and the draft remains only as a legacy
        source citation.
        """
    acceptance {
        check claims-dispositioned {
            statement """
                akr check is clean for the new optimization records; ROADMAP shows the
                optimization track; ACTIVE-WORK lists foundation and bitwriter work.
                """
            method command
            command "akr check"
        }
    }
    part_of [ @jpegxl-rs.track.encoder-optimization ]
    source {
        kind legacy
        path "JPXL/optimization-plan.akr"
        excerpt """
            Encoder assessment and optimization plan (advisor draft converted to AKR).
            """
    }
}

record jpegxl-rs.work.opt-v1-count-only-and-arenas/1 : work {
    title "Opt-V1 count-only pricing and coefficient arenas"
    state superseded
    intent """
        Finish Opt-V1 structural sharing: count-only BitWriter path for exact
        price_codestream without retaining section payloads; group-scoped HF
        coefficient arenas so varblocks share one Arc buffer; reuse quantize
        scratch. Arc plan payloads and Gaborish-once already land. Fixed-input
        codestreams stay byte-identical (Contract A).
        """
    acceptance {
        check contract-a-fingerprint {
            statement """
                vardct-fixed 256 fingerprint remains 37145644e7e1857f after arenas
                and count-only pricing.
                """
            method observation
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.opt-v1-count-only-arenas/1 ]
        }
        check price-matches-emit {
            statement """
                price_codestream sizing equals emit_codestream sizing; unit test
                a_priced_size_is_the_emitted_size_byte_for_byte passes.
                """
            method command
            command "cd JPXL && cargo test -p jpxl-encode a_priced_size_is_the_emitted_size"
            verified_by [ @jpegxl-rs.evidence.opt-v1-count-only-arenas/1 ]
        }
    }
    part_of [ @jpegxl-rs.milestone.m-opt-vardct-structure ]
}

